1. Pull the nginx image from docker hub:
    docker pull nginx
    
2. Run a container from nginx image:
    docker run -d --name my-nginx -p 8080:80 nginx
    
3. List the running containers:
    docker ps
    
4. Go to http://localhost:8080 to see the nginx welcome page.

5. See the details of running nginx container, configration and networking information:
    docker inspect my-nginx

6. To stop the nginx container:
    docker stop my-nginx

7. Verify the list of running comtainer:
    docker ps

8. To start the nginx container again:
    docker start my-nginx

9. To remove the nginx container, first stop the container and then remove.
    docker stop my-nginx
    docker rm my-nginx

10. Verify and see the list of running and stopped containers.
      docker ps -a
